fssimplewindow for RISC OS: a Wimp window drawn through riscos-mesa EGL.

riscos/fsriscoswrapper.cpp (its header comment has the design) and
riscos/fsriscoskeymap.cpp; CMake links GLU, EGL and OSMesa from the
riscos-mesa devkit. Lessons taken from riscos-mesa's freeglut back end and
the other ports:
- one Wimp task; FsPollDevice empties the Wimp queue to the first null
  event every frame; redraws go to eglRedrawWindowRISCOS;
- FsSleep waits in Wimp_PollIdle (UnixLib's sleeps busy-wait in a Wimp
  task and would stop the desktop);
- held keys by an OS_Byte 121 scan while the window has the focus, plus a
  one-poll latch from Key_Pressed so short taps aren't lost; the physical
  key of a Key_Pressed is found by the scan (key numbers from SDL's
  scancodes_riscos.h);
- presses from Mouse_Click at the click's position, releases and movement
  from Wimp_GetPointerInfo, the wheel from OS_Pointer 2;
  Select/Menu/Adjust = left/middle/right;
- full screen = borderless screen-size window (no mode change); pixels vs
  OS units (EX0 EY0 modes); YSFlight$Size and YSFlight$Render (render size,
  EGL_RENDER_*_RISCOS, mouse scaled to it); overlays checked each poll;
- Message_Quit exits; PreQuit is objected to and treated as the close
  icon, and a desktop shutdown is restarted (Wimp_ProcessKey &1FC) if the
  program closes within 30 s; a TaskWindow start is refused with a message;
- GL_PERSPECTIVE_CORRECTION_HINT GL_FASTEST (swrast fast path);
- CLOCK_MONOTONIC (UnixLib 5.0.3.1's HAL counter) for FsSubSecondTimer.

For YSCE ysce_public 1b13297. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

